  <h2 class="heading">Control, Safety & Operating <em>Features</em></h2>
  <p class="copy">
   The OA100 platform includes adjustable door operation, access-control interfaces and monitoring functions. The following features are described in Omega's published technical documentation; some functions are version-dependent.
  </p>

  <div class="feature-grid">
   <article class="feature"><small>01 — CONTROL</small><h3>Universal Digital Controller</h3><p>Digital control board with visual display for setup and programming.</p></article>
   <article class="feature"><small>02 — ACTIVATION</small><h3>Push & Go</h3><p>Selectable function that activates powered operation following manual door movement.</p></article>
   <article class="feature"><small>03 — SAFETY</small><h3>Opening Obstacle Detection</h3><p>Built-in opening-direction obstacle detection. The door stops when it encounters an obstruction and allows closing under standard spring power.</p></article>
   <article class="feature"><small>04 — CLOSING</small><h3>Power Close</h3><p>Selectable function on the XP version to assist positive latching in the programmed latching area.</p></article>
   <article class="feature"><small>05 — POWER</small><h3>On-Board Power Supply</h3><p>24VDC, 1.2A supply for common locks and accessories.</p></article>
   <article class="feature"><small>06 — SPEED</small><h3>Adjustable Door Speed</h3><p>Opening and closing speeds can be adjusted for the installation.</p></article>
   <article class="feature"><small>07 — FORCE</small><h3>Adjustable Closing Force</h3><p>Adjustable closing-force settings for operator configuration.</p></article>
   <article class="feature"><small>08 — ACCESS CONTROL</small><h3>Electric Lock Input</h3><p>Selectable Fail-Safe or Fail-Secure electric lock settings.</p></article>
   <article class="feature"><small>09 — LOCKING</small><h3>Electric Lock Delay</h3><p>Adjustable delay of 0.02–2.0 seconds between electric lock activation and the opening cycle.</p></article>
   <article class="feature"><small>10 — WIND CONTROL</small><h3>Wind Force Dampening</h3><p>Wind Check feature engages the motor to reduce abrupt door speed and help prevent damage to the door, hinges and arms.</p></article>
   <article class="feature"><small>11 — LATCHING</small><h3>Latch Assist</h3><p>Selectable Pull Before Open function helps prevent electric strike binding. Closing latch assist is available with the XP version.</p></article>
   <article class="feature"><small>12 — POSITION</small><h3>Adjustable Latching Area</h3><p>Adjust the latching position and closing speed within the latching area.</p></article>
   <article class="feature"><small>13 — BACK CHECK</small><h3>Adjustable Back Check</h3><p>Set door back-check speed and position for controlled movement.</p></article>
   <article class="feature"><small>14 — MONITORING</small><h3>Open / Closed Status</h3><p>Dry-contact output for monitoring door status.</p></article>
   <article class="feature"><small>15 — SENSORS</small><h3>Presence Detector Inputs</h3><p>Direct inputs for two external presence safety sensors.</p></article>
   <article class="feature"><small>16 — TIMER</small><h3>Hold Open Timer</h3><p>Adjustable hold-open time from 1 to 99 seconds.</p></article>
   <article class="feature"><small>17 — MEMORY</small><h3>Non-Volatile Memory</h3><p>Programmed settings are retained when power is lost.</p></article>
