<section class="section">
 <div class="wrap">
  <div class="eyebrow">Frequently Asked Questions</div>
  <div class="faq-layout">
   <div class="faq-intro">
    <h2 class="heading">Bottom Load Center Hung Operators <em>FAQs</em></h2>
    <p class="copy">
     Find answers to common questions about Omega's OA100-BL Centre Hung Operators, including concealed mounting, model configurations, technical specifications, glass preparation and installation planning.
    </p>
    <p class="copy">
     Need help selecting a CH Series model for your project? Contact Omega to discuss your door arrangement and technical requirements.
    </p>
    <a class="btn" href="https://omegaautomatics.com/contact">Contact Omega</a>
   </div>

   <div class="faq-list">
    <div class="faq-item"><details><summary>What is a bottom load centre hung operator?</summary><p>A bottom load centre hung operator is a concealed automatic swing door operator installed within the door header. The OA100-BL uses a centre-hung arm and bottom pivot arrangement, with the operator spindle acting as the door's top pivot point.</p></details></div>

    <div class="faq-item"><details><summary>What is the difference between centre hung and centre spindle operators?</summary><p>The Centre Hung Series uses a centre-hung arm and bottom pivot, with the operator spindle acting as the top pivot point. The Centre Spindle Series uses a different spindle-drive arrangement. They are separate Omega product configurations and should be selected according to the door design and preparation requirements.</p></details></div>

    <div class="faq-item"><details><summary>What are the benefits of a concealed centre hung operator?</summary><p>The operator is concealed within the door header, avoiding a visible surface-mounted operator box. This arrangement can be useful where overhead clearance is restricted or a clean, uninterrupted transom line is an architectural priority.</p></details></div>

    <div class="faq-item"><details><summary>Which models are available in the CH Series?</summary><p>The OA100-BL Centre Hung Series includes CH-L, CH-R, CH-AA, CH-AM and CH-MA configurations.</p></details></div>

    <div class="faq-item"><details><summary>What is the difference between CH-L and CH-R?</summary><p>CH-L is the single-leaf left-hand configuration, while CH-R is the single-leaf right-hand configuration. Review the corresponding shop drawing to confirm the required handing for your door.</p></details></div>

    <div class="faq-item"><details><summary>What is the CH-AA configuration?</summary><p>CH-AA is the dual Active/Active configuration. Its technical drawing shows two OA100 operators in a dual centre hung arrangement.</p></details></div>

    <div class="faq-item"><details><summary>What are CH-AM and CH-MA configurations?</summary><p>CH-AM is the Active/Monitor arrangement, while CH-MA is Monitor/Active. The published drawings show an OA100 operator paired with a DORMA RTS 88 manual closer for these configurations. Confirm the required arrangement with Omega for your project.</p></details></div>

    <div class="faq-item"><details><summary>Can the Centre Hung Series be used for all-glass entrances?</summary><p>Omega provides a dedicated CH-G centre-hung glass preparation drawing and an arm-mount detail. These documents are relevant when coordinating glass and arm preparation for suitable entrance designs. Confirm the door construction and compatibility with Omega.</p></details></div>

    <div class="faq-item"><details><summary>What is the maximum door weight capacity?</summary><p>The published OA100-BL specification lists a door capacity of up to 450 lbs. Confirm the suitability of the selected configuration against the actual door and installation conditions.</p></details></div>

    <div class="faq-item"><details><summary>What are the header dimensions?</summary><p>The published header dimensions are 4½ inches wide by 4½ inches high. The standard header width is 39 inches for a 36-inch door. Custom widths may be available on request; confirm the final dimensions with Omega.</p></details></div>

    <div class="faq-item"><details><summary>What is the maximum opening angle?</summary><p>The OA100-BL Centre Hung product brochure lists an opening angle of up to 120 degrees. The actual usable opening angle depends on the door, installation and project conditions.</p></details></div>

    <div class="faq-item"><details><summary>What power supply does the operator require?</summary><p>The published power supply requirement is 120VAC, 60Hz. The operator also includes an on-board 24VDC, 1.2A power supply for common locks and accessories.</p></details></div>

    <div class="faq-item"><details><summary>Does the operator support electric locks?</summary><p>Yes. The OA100 documentation lists an electric lock input with selectable Fail-Safe and Fail-Secure settings. It also describes an adjustable electric lock delay. Confirm wiring and compatibility for the selected lock.</p></details></div>

    <div class="faq-item"><details><summary>Does the OA100 include obstacle detection?</summary><p>Yes. The technical feature documentation describes built-in obstacle detection in the opening direction. When the door encounters an obstruction, it stops and allows closing under standard spring power.</p></details></div>

    <div class="faq-item"><details><summary>Are power close and encoder positioning standard features?</summary><p>The technical documentation identifies Power Close and encoder door positioning as XP-version features. Confirm the required version and available functions with Omega before specifying the operator.</p></details></div>

    <div class="faq-item"><details><summary>What finish options are available?</summary><p>The product page highlights Anodized Clear and Anodized Black. The technical drawings also reference clear anodize, dark bronze, light bronze and custom finishes. Contact Omega to confirm the available finish for your selected model.</p></details></div>

    <div class="faq-item"><details><summary>Where can I download Centre Hung technical drawings?</summary><p>Omega provides individual drawings for CH-L, CH-R, CH-AA, CH-AM and CH-MA, along with a CH-G glass preparation detail and a separate arm-mount drawing. The PDF links are available in the Technical Drawings section above.</p></details></div>

    <div class="faq-item"><details><summary>What clear opening is referenced in the CH drawings?</summary><p>The CH-L and CH-R technical drawings reference a 38-inch clear opening to meet ADA requirements. Confirm the applicable accessibility requirements and final clear opening with your project team and local authority.</p></details></div>

    <div class="faq-item"><details><summary>What is the warranty on the OA100-BL operator?</summary><p>The published product specification lists a one-year parts warranty from the date of invoice. Refer to Omega for the applicable warranty terms and conditions.</p></details></div>

